      "pronunciationText": "Start with the rows, called periods. An element's period number is its highest occupied energy level, its outer shell. Across period three, from sodium to argon, every element is filling level three, first three s, then three p. Sodium ends in three s one. Argon ends in three p six, with level three's s and p both full. Then potassium puts its next electron into level four, and a new period begins.",
