      "pronunciationText": "Now the blocks. An element's block tells you the type of subshell its last electron went into. The two columns on the left are the s block. The six on the right are the p block. The ten in the middle are the d block, and the two separate rows underneath are the f block, fourteen wide. That's why the table has this shape. Each block is as wide as the number of electrons its subshell can hold.",
