      ],
      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "The columns are groups, and this is where the pattern really pays off. Valence electrons are the electrons in the outer shell. Down group one, lithium ends in two s one, sodium in three s one, and potassium in four s one. Different levels, but always one valence electron, in an s subshell. Down group seventeen, every element ends in s two, p five, so seven valence electrons. For groups one and two, the number of valence electrons equals the group number. For groups thirteen to eighteen, subtract ten. Helium has two.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
