        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's why groups matter so much. A chemical property describes how a substance reacts to form new substances. A physical property can be observed without making a new substance, like state, colour, or conductivity. Elements in a group share their valence arrangement, so they react in similar ways. Every group one metal reacts with water, making hydrogen gas and an alkaline solution. The halogens in group seventeen are all reactive non-metals, made of pairs of atoms. And the noble gases, with a full outer shell, hardly react at all.",
