        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Let's walk across period three at room temperature. Sodium, magnesium and aluminium are solid metals. Silicon is a solid metalloid. Phosphorus and sulfur are solid non-metals. Then chlorine is a pale green gas, and argon is a colourless gas. So across a period, elements change from metals to non-metals. And across the whole table, only eleven elements are gases at room temperature, and only two are liquids, bromine and mercury. All the rest are solids.",
