      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Selenium is argon, three d ten, four s two, four p four. Its highest level is four, so it's in period four. Its outer shell holds four s two, four p four, which is six valence electrons. The full three d isn't in the outer shell. So it's group sixteen, in the p block. Sulfur, or oxygen, has similar chemistry, because it has the same outer arrangement, s two p four. Putting it in group six is the classic slip.",
