      "pronunciationText": "Last one. Three elements are described by their properties. A is shiny, conducts electricity well, can be hammered into shape, and melts at six hundred and sixty degrees. B is yellow and brittle, doesn't conduct, and melts at a hundred and fifteen degrees. C is shiny grey and brittle, conducts slightly, and melts at fourteen hundred and fourteen degrees. Classify each, and say where each type is found in the periodic table. Pause here to answer.",
